<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech 26-wk T-bill avg yield 11.41 pct (12.37 pct).</title>
<headline>Czech 26-wk T-bill avg yield 11.41 pct (12.37 pct).</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Czech finance ministry 26-week treasury bills hit 11.41 percent, down from 12.37 percent in an auction of similar bills on August 28, the Czech National Bank (CNB) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The auction of 13 billion crowns in T-bills was oversubscribed by 11.31 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Six-month money on the Prague Interbank Offered Rate (PRIBOR) was 12.55 percent on Wednesday.</p>
<p>				   Dec 11	Aug 28</p>
<p> Bids (billion crowns)     24.310	10.101</p>
<p> Bids accepted		 12.999	  5.00</p>
<p> Offer			   13.000	  5.00</p>
<p> Minimum yield (pct)	 11.10	  12.31</p>
<p> Average yield (pct)	 11.408	 12.37</p>
<p> Maximum yield (pct)	 11.51	  12.41</p>
<p> Maturity		     13.06.97    28.02.97</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2422-9857</p>
